    },
    {
      "claim": "Imidafenacin, a basic heterocyclic amide, has 57.8% absolute oral bioavailability in humans, showing that the query's basic piperidine and primary amide do not preclude F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C14","C20","C26","C27","C34","C36","C55","C85"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The phenothiazine analog moricizine shows measurable oral Cmax (1.47 µg/mL after 250 mg) in cirrhotic patients, supporting oral absorption for the phenothiazine class.",
      "card_ids": ["C120"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L3 card provides a direct absolute F value for the query or a transferable sub-20% outcome; the only sub-20% records are rat-specific imidafenacin values and the structurally dissimilar benazeprilat free acid, which do not support F < 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C66","C70","C75","C58","C69"]
    }
  ],
