    "L3 records are oral exposure only and do not quantify F for the query or its closest analogs.",
    "Structural analogy to flupenthixol, trazodone, and moricizine is qualitative; the sulfonyl and piperidine carboxamide groups may alter absorption or metabolism."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is a basic phenothiazine-like amine with a piperidine carboxamide side chain. The most transferable L1 contexts—flupenthixol (30–70%), trazodone (63–91%), and imidafenacin (57.8% human)—all support F ≥ 20%. L3 oral exposure records for trazodone and the phenothiazine analog moricizine show measurable oral plasma exposure, consistent with absorption, but do not provide direct F for the query. No transferable affirmative evidence supports F < 20%; the only sub-20% records are rat-specific or structurally dissimilar. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

